    <string name="fun_bird_instructions">Tap the screen or press A to make Fun Bird flap and stay in the air. Avoid hitting the pipes or the ground. You can pause with the main button and resume anytime.</string>
    <string name="game_fact_fun_bird">Dong Nguyen released Flappy Bird in 2013; its viral difficulty redefined casual games for touch screens.</string>
    <string name="game_fact_snake">Snake became world-famous on the Nokia 6110 in 1997, proving phones could be gaming platforms.</string>
    <string name="game_fact_breakout">Atari released Breakout in 1976 as an evolution of Pong; its development inspired Steve Wozniak to create an ultra-efficient board.</string>
    <string name="game_fact_memory">The modern memory card game was marketed as Concentration in 1959, adapting a traditional children\'s pastime.</string>
    <string name="game_fact_minesweeper">Minesweeper came with Windows in 1990 to teach mouse usage, becoming an office addiction worldwide.</string>
    <string name="game_fact_tictactoe">In 1952, the OXO project at Cambridge University brought Tic-Tac-Toe to a computer, one of the first video games with graphics.</string>
    <string name="game_fact_puzzle">The sliding puzzle 15 Puzzle sparked a craze in 1874, challenging players to arrange tiles by moving only the empty space.</string>
    <string name="game_fact_hangman">The 1894 dictionary already described Hangman as a popular school game, decades before it appeared in children\'s books.</string>
    <string name="game_fact_2048">Gabriele Cirulli created 2048 in 2014 as an open source experiment; within days it became a global logic puzzle phenomenon.</string>
    <string name="game_fact_sudoku">Howard Garns popularized Sudoku in 1979 under the name Number Place, before Japan renamed and exported it worldwide.</string>
    <string name="memory_instructions_text">Find the matching pairs of cards. Tap to flip them and remember their positions to match all pairs!</string>
    <string name="game_2048_instructions_text">Swipe inside the board or move the joystick to slide the tiles. Merge equal numbers to add up. 5×5 board. A new tile appears with each move. Reach the highest score you can.</string>
